      "problem": "If $\\overline{X} = \\{ a, c, d\\}$ and $\\overline{Y} = \\{ a, e, i, o, u \\},$ then what is $\\overline{ X \\cup Y }?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overline{X \\cup Y} \\equiv \\overline{X} \\cap \\overline{Y}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{X\\cup Y} & =\\overset{―}{X}\\cap \\overset{―}{Y} \\\\  & =\\{a,c,d\\}\\cap \\{a,e,i,o,u\\} \\\\  & =\\{a\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
